  "notes": "Cash basis waiver all-funds statement (Exhibit A), period 10/1/21-9/30/22. Page 1a/2a funds blank. General, Street and Senior columns are governmental; Sewer and Water columns are business-type. Solid Waste spending 20,172.45 is printed in the General Fund column (line 45), kept governmental (as FY2023). Transfers (schedule p5): General to Sewer 17,875.86 and Sewer to Water 14,524.74; line 21/52 totals include them. Sewer/Water 'Local Receipts: Other' left other (no breakdown printed; FY2023 took them as utility charges without page evidence). Investments are only in the Sewer/Water funds (CDs: beginning 5,954.68 + 10,680.50; ending Sewer CD 5,978.53 + Water CD 10,717.94, schedule p5), included in the business-type balances. Outstanding loans 469,641.41 (schedule p5) are not on the cash statement, so balance_sheet liabilities are empty. County Treasurer balances (1,421.34 at 10/1/21, 2,375.37 at 9/30/22) printed below the statement, not in the roll-forward. Read pages 1-5 of 5"
